msgctxt "#30021"
msgid "Client version"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30022"
msgid "The YouTube TV web player version this addon claims to be. Google bumps it regularly; a stale value is the likeliest cause of sudden sign-in failures."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30023"
msgid "Licence proxy port"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30024"
msgid "Local port for the Widevine licence proxy. Change it only if something else on this machine already uses it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30025"
msgid "Visitor ID (set automatically)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30026"
msgid "Proof-of-origin token"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30027"
msgid "Google requires a proof-of-origin token on media requests. Without one the CDN refuses every segment. Tokens are tied to a browser session and expire after a few hours."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30033"
msgid "Compare YouTube TV client identities"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30034"
msgid "Before playing, asks every YouTube TV client (web, Android, iOS, TV) for the same video and logs what each is offered. Used to find a client served plain URLs rather than SABR."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30035"
msgid "Probe the SABR endpoint"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30036"
msgid "Before playing, sends a request to the streaming endpoint YouTube's own player uses and logs what comes back. This is where the media actually is; the DASH URLs Kodi can play are refused."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30037"
msgid "JavaScript runtime"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30038"
msgid "Full path to node, deno, bun or quickjs. Needed to compute the n parameter every media URL carries; without it playback is refused. Leave empty to search PATH and the usual locations. Set it explicitly when Kodi is a flatpak or on LibreELEC, where the runtime lives somewhere Kodi does not look."
msgstr ""

